---
layout: layout.njk
ogType: article
---
{#- The only post of a menu tag kept off the home page reads as a page:
    no date, no tag line (blog.json "menu"). -#}
{%- set asPage = menuPages and menuPages[page.inputPath] -%}
<article>
  {#- An untitled note is named for a screen reader by the words its tab
      title uses, never shown: a note has no title on purpose (second pass N12). -#}
  {% if title %}<h1>{{ title }}</h1>{% else %}<h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ content | plainText | noteTitle }}</h1>{% endif %}
  {%- if not asPage %}
  {#- The date, the tags (each once; a menu list's tag in the menu's words,
      linking to its list) and the post's own author, when it has one that
      is not the blog's (second pass N17: the blog's author on every post
      of a one-author blog was noise). -#}
  {%- set line = tags | tagLine %}
  <p class="meta"><time datetime="{{ date | isoDate }}">{{ date | readableDate }}</time>{% for t in line %}{% if loop.first %} · {% endif %}{% if t.url %}<a href="{{ t.url | url }}">{{ t.label }}</a>{% else %}{{ t.label }}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if author and author != blog.author %} · <span class="by">{{ author }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
  {%- endif %}
  {{ content | safe }}
</article>
{# Machine-readable twin of the article, for search results. #}
{%- set words = content | plainText %}
<script type="application/ld+json">{{ {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage' if asPage else 'BlogPosting',
  headline: title or (words | noteTitle),
  datePublished: undefined if asPage else (date | isoDate),
  description: description or (content | leadSentence) or undefined,
  url: site.url + page.url if site.url else page.url,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: (author if author and author != blog.author else blog.author) or blog.title }
} | jsonld | safe }}</script>
